{"_meta":{"source":"Yahoo Finance via yfinance (profile, statements, analyst estimates)","fetched_at":"2026-10-22T15:55:13+00:00","status":"ok","error":null,"last_success":"2026-10-22T15:55:13+00:00"},"data":{"profile":{"name":"Voestalpine AG","sector":"Basic Materials","industry":"Steel","country":"Austria","city":"Linz","website":"https://www.voestalpine.com","employees":48641,"summary":"Voestalpine AG processes, develops, manufactures, and sells steel and technology products in Austria, the European Union, and internationally. It operates through five divisions: Steel Division, High Performance Metals Division, Metal Engineering Division, Metal Forming Division, and Holding & Group Services. The Steel division produces hot and cold-rolled steel strips, as well as electrogalvanized, hot-dip galvanized, and organically coated steel strips; heavy plates, and foundry products for the energy sector; and turbine casings. The High Performance Metals division offers special high-alloy tool and high-speed steel for the oil and natural gas, aerospace, and energy engineering industries; utilizing nickel-base and titanium alloys; tool manufacturing, component processing, heat treatment, and coating services; warehousing and preprocessing of special steels; and various services, including logistics, distribution, and processing for the oil and natural gas industries. The Metal Engineering division provides wire rods and drawn wires, seamless tubes for special applications, and welding consumables and machinery; rails and digital monitoring systems; and services related to rail infrastructure. The Metal Forming segment manufactures refined special sections, tubes, and precision strip steel products; pre-finished system components made from pressed, punched, and roll-profiled parts; and storage system solutions for manufacturers in the automotive production and supply industries, as well as various companies in the commercial vehicle, construction, storage, energy, and agricultural machinery industries. It serves automotive, energy, railway systems, construction, mechanical engineering, white goods/consumer goods, aerospace, and other industries. Voestalpine AG is headquartered in Linz, Austria.","exchange":"Vienna","currency":"EUR","financial_currency":"EUR","summary_fr":"Voestalpine AG traite, développe, fabrique et vend des produits sidérurgiques et technologiques en Autriche, dans l’Union européenne et à l’international. Elle opère à travers cinq divisions : Steel Division, High Performance Metals Division, Metal Engineering Division, Metal Forming Division et Holding & Group Services. La division Steel produit des bandes d'acier laminées à chaud et à froid, ainsi que des bandes d'acier électrogalvanisées, galvanisées à chaud et revêtues d'un revêtement organique; des tôles lourdes et des produits de fonderie pour le secteur de l'énergie; et des carters de turbines."},"valuation":{"market_cap_yahoo":7152920064,"shares_outstanding":171450616,"trailing_pe":14.094595,"forward_pe":8.187344,"price_to_book":0.91553473,"ev_to_ebitda":5.873,"ev_to_revenue":0.577,"dividend_yield":0.0172,"payout_ratio":0.2027,"beta_yahoo":1.806},"targets":{"current_price":41.72,"mean":54.41,"median":53.65,"high":64.0,"low":46.0,"n_analysts":10,"reco_mean":2.2,"reco_key":"buy"},"calendar":{"earnings_dates":["2026-11-11"],"eps_avg":0.59214,"eps_low":0.58,"eps_high":0.60692,"revenue_avg":3880039780,"ex_dividend":"2026-07-09","dividend_date":"1970-08-23"},"holders":{"insiders_pct":0.28465998,"institutions_pct":0.29955998,"institutions_float_pct":0.41877,"institutions_n":203,"institutions":[{"name":"Pacer Advisors, Inc.","pct":0.0,"shares":555,"value":23154,"date":"2024-12-31","chg":-0.059299998}],"funds":[{"name":"VANGUARD STAR FUNDS-Vanguard Total International Stock Index Fund","pct":0.0099,"shares":1762664,"value":73538344,"date":"2026-07-31","chg":0.0087},{"name":"VANGUARD TAX-MANAGED FUNDS-Vanguard Developed Markets Index Fund","pct":0.0064999997,"shares":1165